  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caring for Mothers&#x2019; Lives -WeCare</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;b&gt;The WeCare project&lt;/b&gt;, Caring for Mothers&#x2019; Lives aims to guarantee the right to safe, quality education and healthcare in a more transparent way, particularly for vulnerable groups, including children, girls and women, as well as refugees. It will strengthen 3 complementary dimensions: demand, supply and governance of services.     On the demand side, the objective is that rights-holders increase their autonomy and demand equitable and timely access to health care (Result 1).   On the supply side, the aim is that duty-bearers ensure increasing inclusive access to quality SRHR services (Results 2 and 3).   On the governance side, the objective is that rights-holders and duty-bearers adopt participatory governance and shared accountability for managing their local health services (Results 4 and 5).</narrative>
  </description>
